    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0428" n="1388" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1388"/>

                <head>No. 932.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Viscount das
                        Nogueiras.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 21,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Viscount</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 22d ultimo, and to say in reply that as I am
                    informed by the Secretary of the Treasury the practice in exempting from duty
                    supplies, <pb facs="0429" n="1389" xml:id="pg1389"/> etc., for foreign vessels
                    of war, is governed by section 2982 of the Revised Statutes, and the privilege
                    is only extended to the vessels of war of such nations as reciprocate towards
                    vessels of war of the United States while in the ports of such nations.” I
                    inclose a copy of the statutory provision.</p>
                <p>Accept, Viscount, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
